{"id": "EUVD-2026-103779", "enisaUuid": "b44d8883-d1e0-31a6-89f6-428a012b705a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvt: selection: Fix unsigned underflow and slab-out-of-bounds read in paste_selection()\n\nIn paste_selection(), the loop copies min_t(unsigned int,\nvc_sel.buf_len - pasted,tty->receive_room) bytes per iteration into\ntty_ldisc_receive_buf() and increments pasted += count.\n\nBecause the selection mutex (vc_sel.lock) is dropped inside the loop\nWhenever the line discipline buffer fills up and paste_selection()\nsleeps on tty->write_wait, a concurrent TIOCLINUX (TIOCL_SETSEL) ioctl\ncan replace vc_sel.buffer with a shorter selection and reduce\nvc_sel.buf_len below pasted.\n\nWhen paste_selection() resumes, vc_sel.buf_len - pasted underflows as an\nunsigned integer to a large positive value, causing\ntty_ldisc_receive_buf(ld, vc_sel.buffer + pasted, NULL, count) to read\nup to 4094 bytes out-of-bounds past the newly allocated vc_sel.buffer.\n\nFix this by terminating the loop when pasted >= vc_sel.buf_len.\n\nKernel stack trace (Linux 7.3.0-rc3):\n ==================================================================\n BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in n_tty_receive_buf_common+0xa01/0x1650\n Read of size 4094 at addr ffff888101c58010 by task kworker/u17:1/65\n Workqueue: events_unbound flush_to_ldisc\n Call Trace:\n  <TASK>\n  dump_stack_lvl+0x70/0xa0\n  print_report+0x153/0x4c6\n  kasan_report+0xf1/0x120\n  kasan_check_range+0x11c/0x200\n  __asan_memcpy+0x29/0x70\n  n_tty_receive_buf_common+0xa01/0x1650\n  tty_ldisc_receive_buf+0x66/0x110\n  tty_port_default_receive_buf+0x6b/0xb0\n  flush_to_ldisc+0x1b4/0x410\n  process_one_work+0x6ff/0x1110\n  worker_thread+0x4a8/0xb70\n  kthread+0x307/0x3e0\n  ret_from_fork+0x3ed/0x680\n  </TASK>\n ==================================================================", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:50:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:26:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/037d7e3ca5c593092f4b0d471eb869a85cbddde0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/619c6d7dd76fff15a9714fbf02ce299b737f01a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39495ef5d6f8019e62d65807f217a7ca8232727a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98839", "GHSA-rgr5-hhj8-qq6p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "077ff34d-6c20-39f8-9097-013b355c4a67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9.216 <4.10"}, {"id": "1348a8b6-c1ed-342d-9052-fa0d2e812e65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e8c75a30a23c6ba63f4ef6895cbf41fd42f21aa2 <619c6d7dd76fff15a9714fbf02ce299b737f01a2"}, {"id": "1ff6e0d7-432b-3153-94d8-56c1d04f09ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e5be0e24ffc7f5783a3864b5b958088ed15be9e8"}, {"id": "41a81292-d13f-397f-93ba-b8bce25b7c22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e8c75a30a23c6ba63f4ef6895cbf41fd42f21aa2 <39495ef5d6f8019e62d65807f217a7ca8232727a"}, {"id": "482b439a-c98f-3bd6-a661-3230977a80c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.16.83 <3.17"}, {"id": "4d9dee61-c4b1-3580-b6be-de4065b8f3a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.25 <5.5"}, {"id": "6012d60d-d802-3210-9a49-744e5ef87396", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "67a0aabd-197d-3341-a405-3561a6e73fac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "54c522782fd11a720f959ee9cb5a15bb9580343d"}, {"id": "773615c7-86ba-352b-bc75-bd4d7cd650a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "05c508edc9d0b44e4706d3c2cf14ee12aac210d2"}, {"id": "7ca5b386-8368-31af-850e-1b985b69b9dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.4.216 <4.5"}, {"id": "8231718a-89b4-3623-bcea-728486267b36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8c368d36878e2fc99285279fc5e14b3d3cb8947c"}, {"id": "8a3e473b-5a41-30b1-8c1e-296b0b218916", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "8d508a28-ce56-3746-a905-c7d185b53fc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "90b5e8f7-acf8-3fb9-ace8-1da560ae1237", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "a7d0f962-3842-314e-b9a7-1fd4f0a92db7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19.109 <4.20"}, {"id": "acd0d37f-b6d8-32fb-9869-8977c1844257", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b4492f1e7456bd162714c0ec2815c2749d930844"}, {"id": "c35b079a-c745-3fa9-97f4-646769463b2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c925926c-a496-3b11-8517-71aa605d3031", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9a9c13ad21a8220cb70c9807a920f43520515f94"}, {"id": "d4126f14-25e9-3e6b-9e1e-7378d600f2cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a4719f6d07b2c63223f7452c435c5f578f105cfe"}, {"id": "e1936240-ab9a-3f15-a3b5-f2241a5fdd54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.5.9 <5.6"}, {"id": "e81f1e77-b4fb-3830-808d-6ae577d211b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e8c75a30a23c6ba63f4ef6895cbf41fd42f21aa2 <037d7e3ca5c593092f4b0d471eb869a85cbddde0"}, {"id": "f0893468-ced1-3181-a39b-4c140432db4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.14.173 <4.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "41299ae7-3303-3323-b179-f901ff9d7736", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}